      body: "Book the first visit when the first tooth appears, or by your child's first birthday. Early visits are about prevention, and they let your child get used to the clinic before anything needs treating.\n\nThe first visit is short. Your child usually sits on your lap. The dentist counts the teeth, looks at the gums, and checks for early signs of decay, often the white chalky lines that appear before a cavity.\n\nMost of the time is spent with you: how to brush a toddler's teeth, how much toothpaste to use (a smear the size of a rice grain under three), and why a bottle of milk at bedtime is a common cause of decay in milk teeth.\n\nMilk teeth matter. They hold space for the adult teeth, and a painful milk tooth affects eating, sleep and school. After the first visit, a check every six months is usual.",
